# Files EAS Build should NOT upload to the cloud builder.
#
# EAS uses this file INSTEAD of .gitignore when it exists. That lets us keep
# google-services.json out of GitHub (still listed in .gitignore) while STILL
# shipping it to our own private EAS build, which needs it: it is required by
# android.googleServicesFile at prebuild. It is referenced here only by its
# ABSENCE — anything not listed uploads.
#
# .env is deliberately NOT uploaded. Build-time values come from the EAS
# environment bound to each profile in eas.json ("environment": development |
# preview | production). Uploading .env as well would leave two sources for the
# same variables and make it ambiguous which one a build actually used — the
# exact way a production build could end up quietly pointing at the test stack.
# .env stays on disk for local `expo start`.

# Dependencies & build output (don't upload — EAS reinstalls/rebuilds)
node_modules/
.expo/
dist/
web-build/
.git/

# Dev cruft
.metro-health-check*
*.tsbuildinfo
.DS_Store
npm-debug.*
yarn-debug.*
yarn-error.*
app-example

# Local-only environment values (see the header). Globbed so that a future
# .env.local or .env.production can't start leaking into builds unnoticed.
.env*

# NEVER upload signing / service-account secrets
*.jks
*.p8
*.p12
*.key
*.mobileprovision
*-firebase-adminsdk-*.json
play-service-account*.json
